<title>UK: NWE gasoline gains trimmed by soft NYMEX.</title>
<headline>NWE gasoline gains trimmed by soft NYMEX.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spot gasoline prices in NWE traded firmer in early business on Monday but weaker afternoon NYMEX gasoline futures trimmed gains, traders said.</p>
<p>Cargo activity in northwest Europe remained extremely light with demand from inland markets staying thin and transatlantic trade muted.</p>
<p>Prompt Eurograde barges on the ARA market traded at $221.50, $221.25 and $221 fob Rotterdam.</p>
<p>-- Colin Wooster, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7456</p>
</text>
